# Security

## Always check for

### Injection

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — direct user input in query
Beat.find({ title: req.query.title });

// ✅ GOOD — Zod-parsed, typed input
const { title } = searchSchema.parse(params);
Beat.find({ title: { $regex: escapeRegex(title), $options: "i" } });
```

- Never interpolate user input into database queries.
- Always parse with Zod before using in queries.
- Escape regex special characters.

### XSS

- React auto-escapes JSX — never use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with user input.
- Sanitize any content rendered from the database that could contain HTML.
- Use `Content-Security-Policy` headers.

### CSRF

- State-changing operations require authentication.
- Razorpay webhooks: verify HMAC signature with `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET`.

### Rate limiting

- All public POST/PATCH/DELETE endpoints.
- Auth endpoints (login, signup, password reset).
- Use `getClientIp` + `rateLimit` from `@/lib/security/rate-limit`.

### Secrets & environment

- Never commit `.env` files.
- Never log secrets or tokens.
- Validate `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` vars don't contain server secrets.
- PII: minimize storage, encrypt at rest, audit access.

### Secure headers

- `Strict-Transport-Security`, `X-Content-Type-Options`, `X-Frame-Options`.
- Cookie settings: `httpOnly`, `secure`, `sameSite`.
